{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Transportation to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents \r\n relative to Class 3 bikes/RTAs,\r\n\r\n","BillNumber":"S2852","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J27","Name":"Joint Committee on Transportation","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27","ResponseDate":"2024-07-01T11:12:32.703"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2852/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"Senate, July 3, 2024 -- The committee on Transportation, to whom was referred the petitions (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2230) of Sal N. DiDomenico and Michael J. Barrett for legislation relative to class 3 electric bicycles; and (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2277) of Susan L. Moran, Joanne M. Comerford, Jack Patrick Lewis, Susannah M. Whipps and other members of the General Court for legislation to increase regional transit accessibility in the Commonwealth, report the accompanying Order (Senate, No. 2852).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Transportation be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents numbered 2230 and 2277 relative to Class 3 bikes/RTAs.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}